{"id":"ess-c5-justice-2","audio":"trabajo/clips/ess-c5-justice-2/audio.mp3","duracion":22.92,"escena":{"id":"c5-justice","hilo":"sostenibilidad","unidad":"1.3 Justice","titulo":"Environmental justice","claves":["Exposure","Voice","Remedy"],"visual":{"tipo":"tabla","titulo":"Named cases","columnas":["Case","What happened","Who carried the cost"],"filas":[["Bhopal, 1984","Toxic gas leak, pesticide plant","Poor settlements beside the plant"],["Grassy Narrows","Mercury in the river, 1962–1970","Anishinaabe community: food, jobs, culture"],["Agbogbloshie","Burning e-waste for copper","Workers, including children"],["Doñana, 1998","Aznalcóllar tailings dam burst","Damage clear; injustice mainly economic"]]},"inicio":0,"fin":22.92,"turnos":[{"q":"H","t":"Is every disaster an injustice, though?","inicio":0.35,"fin":3.2},{"q":"E","t":"That's the nine-mark discuss question. Distinguish damage from injustice. Ask three questions: unequal exposure, unequal voice and unequal remedy. In Doñana the damage is clear, but evidence of discrimination is weak; the possible injustice is economic, because public administrations paid much of the clean-up.","inicio":3.35,"fin":22.32}]},"desfase":39.59,"durEscena":63.51,"parte":{"n":2,"de":2},"materia":"ESS","nombres":{"H":"Sonia","E":"Ryan"}}